  "thumbnailAlt": "Sports Registration form beside a photo of boys playing a soccer match on a sunny day",
  "content": {
    "intro": "A sports registration form is a form that collects a player's details, age division, experience level, uniform size, emergency contact and medical notes, plus an acknowledgement of risk, so a league or club can build balanced teams for the season. This template works for youth leagues with a parent or guardian filling it in and for adult leagues where players sign themselves up.",
    "audience": "Youth soccer, basketball, baseball and netball leagues, community sports clubs, rec departments and adult social leagues.",
    "useCases": [
      "Spring or fall season sign-up for a youth soccer league",
      "Adult rec basketball or volleyball league registration",
      "Club tryout registration before team selection",
      "Summer clinic or skills program sign-up"
    ],
    "tips": [
      "Export registrations to Excel and sort by division and experience to draft balanced teams.",
      "Use conditional logic to show the parent or guardian section only when the player is under 18.",
      "Set a response limit per form in Form Settings so registration closes when the season's roster spots are filled."
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "What should a sports registration form include?",
        "answer": "The player's name and date of birth, division or age group, experience level and position, jersey size, parent or guardian contact for minors, an emergency contact, medical conditions or allergies, and agreement to the league's code of conduct and risk acknowledgement."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do leagues place players in age divisions?",
        "answer": "Most youth leagues place players by their age on a set cutoff date or by birth year, as set by their governing body. Asking for date of birth lets you check each player's division before you build teams."
      },
      {
        "question": "Is the consent section in this template a legal waiver?",
        "answer": "It is a plain-language acknowledgement of risk with a typed name and a consent box. Waiver rules differ by state, country and sport, so have the wording reviewed for your local rules and your insurer's requirements."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can parents register more than one child?",
        "answer": "Yes. Parents submit the form once per child, which keeps each player's medical notes and division separate in your responses and exports."
      }
    ]
  },
